.TH ETHERAPE2026 1 "November 2026" "EtherApe 2026 1.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
etherape2026 \- graphical network traffic monitor (Qt 6 port of EtherApe)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B etherape2026
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B etherape2026
displays network activity graphically. It captures packets with libpcap (Npcap
on Windows), decodes them and draws a live graph of the hosts and the links
between them, with per-protocol colours and traffic statistics.
.PP
Nodes can be grouped into network zones (LAN, DMZ, VPN, Internet) and merged
across IPv4 and IPv6 when they share a MAC address. Capture files can be
replayed, and the graph exported as XML or JSON.
.PP
Live capture requires privileges: either run as root, grant
.B cap_net_raw,cap_net_admin
to the binary with
.BR setcap ,
or let the application elevate a small helper through
.BR pkexec .
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-i ", \-\-interface " device
Capture on
.IR device .
Under Linux, "any" captures on all interfaces at once (Linux cooked capture).
.TP
.BI \-r ", \-\-replay " file
Replay packets from a pcap file instead of capturing live.
.TP
.BI \-f ", \-\-filter " bpf
Apply a BPF capture filter (for example "tcp port 443"). Packets that do not
match are dropped by libpcap.
.TP
.BI \-m ", \-\-mode " link|ip|tcp
Granularity of the nodes: MAC addresses, IP addresses, or address:port pairs.
Default: ip.
.TP
.B \-\-show " expression"
Display filter. Hides nodes and links without touching the capture.
Space-separated terms, written with ':' or '=': proto:http, host:10.0.0 or
hostname=laptop, vlan:100, zone:dmz, or free text; prefix a term with '-' to
exclude it. Key aliases: proto/protocol, host/hostname/name/node/ip/addr,
vlan/vid, zone/cloud. The input field autocompletes known keys, protocols,
zones, VLANs and node names.
.TP
.B \-n ", \-\-numeric"
Keep addresses numeric: no reverse DNS lookups.
.TP
.BI \-\-node\-limit " count"
Keep at most
.I count
nodes in the graph (default 300).
.TP
.BI \-\-speed " percent"
Replay speed, in percent of the recorded pace (0 = as fast as possible).
.TP
.BI \-\-final\-export " file"
Export the graph to
.I file
at the end of a replay and exit. The format follows the extension: \&.xml
or \&.json.
.TP
.BI \-\-position " file"
Load a node layout (JSON) saved from the interface.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/etherape/etherape2026.conf
User settings (language, zones, filters, window geometry).
.TP
.I /etc/ethers
Optional static MAC to name mapping, read at start-up.
.TP
.I /dev/shm/etherape2026-<uid>/helper-*.log
Diagnostic output of the privileged capture helper (removed at exit).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR pcap (3),
.BR tcpdump (8),
.BR setcap (8),
.BR pkexec (1)
.PP
Project page: https://gitlab.com/rghetta/etherape
